{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_7tmm5fpz6ajtzdtlj7ohi5fzbf7bb3zhwcdgxpr47ftwz672765a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both files written.\n\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-li83Jg/_logs/frag/G3_errors.md` — 123 rows\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-li83Jg/_logs/frag/G3_configs.md` — 229 rows\n\nKey findings worth flagging for the differential-testing plan:\n\n1. **`crypto_hash_sha3_384` does not exist** in 1.0.23. Only `crypto_hash_sha3256` (rate 136) and `crypto_hash_sha3512` (rate 72) are exported. Drop it from the plan.\n2. **`crypto_generichash_*_final` has no `outlen` validation in the wrapper** — bad `outlen` reaches `blake2b_final` and triggers `sodium_misuse()` (abort), not `-1`. `outlen >= 256` is silently truncated to `(uint8_t)outlen` in NDEBUG builds, so e.g. `outlen=288` returns 0 and writes 32 bytes. Also `final`'s `outlen` is never checked against `init`'s `outlen`.\n3. **The only state-misuse guard in blake2b** is `blake2b_is_lastblock()` in `blake2b_final` → `-1` on double-final. There is no guard on `update` after `final`.\n4. **SHA3/SHAKE/TurboSHAKE soft errors**: `_update` after squeeze/final returns `-1` *but still absorbs the input* after silently permuting and resetting the phase; `sha3_final` called twice returns `-1` but still writes output. `_squeeze` never returns `-1`.\n5. **HMAC init NULL-check ordering bug**: `key == NULL && keylen > 64` (sha256) / `> 128` (sha512) takes the key-pre-hashing branch first, bypassing the `sodium_misuse()` NULL check → NULL deref. Same bug propagates into `crypto_kdf_hkdf_*_extract_init` with a NULL salt and large `salt_len`.\n6. **`crypto_kdf_blake2b_derive_from_key` copies `ctx` before the `subkey_len` bound check**, so a NULL `ctx` faults even on calls that would return `-1`.\n7. Documented minimums are **not enforced** by `crypto_generichash*`: `outlen` 1..15 and `keylen` 1..15 are accepted despite `BYTES_MIN`/`KEYBYTES_MIN` being 16. Only `outlen==0`, `outlen>64`, `keylen>64` are rejected.\n8. **XOF domain byte is unvalidated** — `0x00` and `0x80`..`0xFF` are accepted; `domain=0x80` XORs to `0x00` in the `offset == rate-1` single-byte pad branch.\n9. Resolved limits: `crypto_kdf_hkdf_sha256_BYTES_MAX` = 8160, `_sha512_BYTES_MAX` = 16320, `BYTES_MIN` = 0 for both; `crypto_kdf_blake2b` 16/64/ctx 8/key 32; shake128 & turboshake128 rate 168, shake256 & turboshake256 rate 136, sha3-256 rate 136, sha3-512 rate 72, all `DOMAIN_STANDARD` = 0x1F, all `STATEBYTES` = 256.\n10. `crypto_shorthash`, `crypto_onetimeauth_poly1305` (except `_verify`), `crypto_hash_sha256/512`, and all `crypto_auth_*` non-verify entry points have **zero rejection paths** — they always return 0, so differential testing there is purely about output bytes."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":225,"cache_read_input_tokens":104422,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":225,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_017iRL1x3udqRRLsB1gFYyxB","session_id":"37babf23-64fa-4bd5-8c90-ef1a4034e89f","uuid":"036e1468-3abc-4e4d-9cb0-ed91aba470a8","timestamp":"2026-09-08T15:11:59.261Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Enumerate hash/generichash/auth error/config"}
