{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_mgiwn3546p5k5kbpjzawx26casxroz65ryh2ujxzm7arajewbwaa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-li83Jg/_logs/frag/G2_errors.md — 182 rows\n/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-li83Jg/_logs/frag/G2_configs.md — 117 rows\n\nKey findings worth relaying:\n\n- **Argon2 internal enums are fully erased at the public boundary.** Every `ARGON2_*` code (-1..-35) collapses to `return -1`. Only `ARGON2_VERIFY_MISMATCH` (-35) additionally sets `errno = EINVAL`; all other decode/validate failures leave `errno` untouched. A Rust port must not set errno on malformed-string paths.\n- **Two abort paths:** `crypto_pwhash_str_alg` with `alg ∉ {1,2}` calls `sodium_misuse()` (abort, not -1), and `escrypt_PBKDF2_SHA256` with `dkLen > 0x1fffffffe0` calls `sodium_misuse()`.\n- **Asymmetric OPSLIMIT_MIN:** argon2i = 3, argon2id = 1. `crypto_pwhash` with `alg=1, opslimit=1` fails EINVAL while `alg=2, opslimit=1` succeeds.\n- **`memlimit` is truncated by `/1024U`** before becoming `m_cost`, so memlimit 8192 and 8193 must produce *identical* digests, and `str_needs_rehash` returns 0 for memlimit differences under 1024. This is a high-value differential case.\n- **scrypt one-shot does NOT range-check opslimit/memlimit.** `pickparams` silently clamps opslimit up to 32768 and accepts memlimit=0 (yielding N=2). So `crypto_pwhash_scryptsalsa208sha256(..., opslimit=0, memlimit=0)` succeeds — unlike every argon2 entry point. `scrypt_..._str_verify` also skips passwdlen checks entirely and requires `strlen(str) == 101` exactly.\n- **Encoding surface:** `$v=` is *mandatory* and must be exactly 19 (0x13); `v=16` → `ARGON2_INCORRECT_TYPE` (-26), not DECODING_FAIL. Base64 is `ORIGINAL_NO_PADDING`, so `=` padding causes the subsequent `$`/EOS check to fail → DECODING_FAIL. Leading zeros in m/t/p/v are rejected by `decode_decimal`. Passing an `$argon2id$` string to the argon2i decoder yields DECODING_FAIL (prefix `$argon2i` matches, then `d$v=` fails).\n- **lanes > 1 is unreachable via public hashing APIs** (`parallelism` is hardcoded to 1); `p=2/4` is only reachable through `argon2_decode_string` in `*_str_verify` / `*_str_needs_rehash`. That is the only way to test `ARGON2_MEMORY_TOO_LITTLE` from `m_cost < 8*lanes`.\n- Dead branches identified (should be noted so the Rust port isn't tested against them): every `PASSWD_MIN` check (MIN=0), `ARGON2_PWD_TOO_SHORT`, `AD_*`, `SECRET_*`, `THREADS_TOO_*` (shadowed by LANES checks), all `pickparams() != 0` paths, and the post-`DECIMAL_U32` `> UINT32_MAX` re-checks in the decoder.\n\nThe configs file's trailing HTML comment lists the too-slow combinations (SENSITIVE/MODERATE profiles, RFC 7914 vector 4, MEMLIMIT_MAX, outlen near BYTES_MAX) plus the cheapest params that still exercise each path — notably argon2id `opslimit=1, memlimit=8192` and scrypt `_ll N=2, r=1, p=1`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":225,"cache_read_input_tokens":121127,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":225,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_012wRW78gcew7k2BdauggP85","session_id":"37babf23-64fa-4bd5-8c90-ef1a4034e89f","uuid":"a0a30e4d-30d1-44fa-aa6e-798eacea2e8d","timestamp":"2026-09-08T15:12:16.958Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Enumerate pwhash error/config surface"}
