{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_6ivwjr4j6fazzrzxqpiqdwvmhjdh664utlwprrmwghwgzvxq4x2q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-li83Jg/_logs/frag/G6_errors.md — 101 rows\n/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-li83Jg/_logs/frag/G6_configs.md — 107 rows\n\nKey findings worth relaying:\n\n- **No IP-string API exists.** `crypto_ipcrypt_str_to_ip16` / `ip16_to_str` and any `inet_pton`/`inet_ntop` usage are absent from the entire tree; `crypto_ipcrypt.h` exposes only the 16-byte binary API. That whole parsing surface in the brief is non-existent.\n- **crypto_ipcrypt has zero error paths** — every entry point returns `void`, with no key/tweak/length checks. There IS an undocumented **pfx** variant (`_pfx_keygen/_pfx_encrypt/_pfx_decrypt`, PFX_KEYBYTES=32) not in the brief, plus a data-dependent degenerate-key branch in ndx/pfx (when the two key halves yield equal middle round keys, k2 is re-derived from `k[i] ^ 0x5a`) that must be mirrored in Rust.\n- **Naming corrections**: libsodium uses `*_seed_keypair` and `*_enc_deterministic`, not `_keypair_derand`/`_enc_derand`; and `randombytes_stir`/`randombytes_close`, not `randombytes_random_stir`/`_close`. Asymmetric seed sizes: mlkem768 seed_keypair=64 B / enc_deterministic=32 B; xwing seed_keypair=32 B / enc_deterministic=64 B.\n- **Only real KEM `-1` paths**: `mlkem768_ref_enc_deterministic` rejects a non-canonical pk (any 12-bit coeff ≥ 3329) — reachable with `pk[0]=pk[1]=0xff`; and `crypto_kem_xwing_enc/dec` return -1 when X25519 yields an all-zero shared secret (low-order point in `pk[1184..1216]` or `ct[1088..1120]`). The xwing→mlkem dec failure branch is dead code.\n- **Implicit rejection precisely**: `mlkem768_ref_dec` never returns -1. `fail = sodium_memcmp(ct, cmp, 1088)`, `fail_mask = (unsigned)fail >> 31`, and `cmov` swaps in `k_bar = SHAKE256(z ‖ ct)[0..32]` with `z = sk[2368..2400]`. There is **no** hpk consistency check — a tampered `sk[2336..2368]` silently degrades to implicit rejection. This makes corrupted-ciphertext decap a hard byte-equality assertion, not a \"both fail\" one.\n- **randombytes_set_implementation never validates** (returns 0 even for NULL or for a struct with NULL \"required\" hooks), which is the sanctioned determinism hook; both shipped impls set `.uniform = NULL`, so the default rejection loop is always exercised. `randombytes_uniform(0)` and `(1)` return 0 without consuming randomness. `randombytes_buf_deterministic` aborts via `sodium_misuse()` only for size > 274877906944 (64-bit builds).\n- The bulk of the randombytes error surface is platform-conditional `sodium_misuse()`/`assert()` aborts (entropy-source failure, fork detection via `global.pid != getpid()`, `size == 0` tripping `assert(chunk_size > 0)` in the getrandom/getentropy chunking wrappers)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2147,"cache_read_input_tokens":104838,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2147,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01UwFaLP6CiirK4gAc1ZYBnq","session_id":"37babf23-64fa-4bd5-8c90-ef1a4034e89f","uuid":"e516faf2-a9fc-4a1c-b486-5c916b4830b8","timestamp":"2026-09-08T15:12:43.369Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Enumerate randombytes/kem/ipcrypt error/config"}
