{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_zblzg527fnp2ncnvylkzratqlh6vyevmhnjfoqhyyr5sgvk6hbjq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both files written (read-only pass over the C source; no source files modified).\n\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-li83Jg/_logs/frag/G5_errors.md` — **130 rows**\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-li83Jg/_logs/frag/G5_configs.md` — **172 rows** (plus the trailing HTML comment on non-determinism)\n\nKey findings worth flagging to the plan:\n\n- **`crypto_core_ed25519_from_uniform` / `from_hash` do not exist in 1.0.23's public header.** The map-to-curve surface is `crypto_core_ed25519_from_string{,_nu}(ctx, msg, hash_alg)`; `ge25519_from_uniform`/`ge25519_from_hash` are internal only. `crypto_core_ristretto255_from_hash` *does* still exist.\n- **Neither `ED25519_NONDETERMINISTIC` nor `ED25519_COMPAT` is defined** in this tree, so signing is fully deterministic (byte-comparable) and the `sig[63] & 224` branch in `open.c:31` is dead code — the live check is `(sig[63] & 240) != 0 && sc25519_is_canonical(sig+32) == 0`.\n- **Inconsistent validation between sibling functions** — three likely divergence sites: `crypto_core_ed25519_add/sub` do *only* `frombytes` + `is_on_curve` (they accept non-canonical `edff..7f` encodings, the identity, and small-order points, unlike `is_valid_point`); `crypto_sign_ed25519_pk_to_curve25519` omits the `ge25519_is_canonical` check that `verify_detached` performs; `crypto_core_ed25519_scalar_invert` only tests literal byte-zero, so `s = L` returns 0 with a meaningless `recip`.\n- `crypto_scalarmult_ed25519(n=0)` still **writes `q`** before returning -1 (`t` aliases `q`, and clamping makes the internal scalar nonzero) — an easy place for a Rust port to differ.\n- `crypto_box_curve25519xchacha20poly1305` has **no NaCl zero-padded API** (no ZEROBYTES/BOXZEROBYTES/`_afternm` classic form); only xsalsa20 has it, and that