{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_fxfjsk42czzheuhj256eejh4u2d6nwnz4ekt2uvqa3ztpspwjtna","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_0167ztcgEAF2qnUMRc1CDQot","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"W=/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-li83Jg; L=$W/_logs\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport re,os\nL=\"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-li83Jg/_logs\"\nT=\"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-li83Jg/translation\"\ngroups=[(\"G1\",\"sodium/utils.c, codecs.c, core.c, runtime.c, version.c; crypto_verify/\"),\n        (\"G2\",\"crypto_pwhash/ (argon2 + argon2-encoding + scryptsalsa208sha256 + pbkdf2)\"),\n        (\"G3\",\"crypto_generichash/, crypto_shorthash/, crypto_onetimeauth/, crypto_auth/, crypto_kdf/, crypto_hash/, crypto_xof/, crypto_core/keccak1600\"),\n        (\"G4\",\"crypto_aead/, crypto_secretbox/, crypto_secretstream/, crypto_stream/, crypto_core/{salsa,hsalsa20,hchacha20}\"),\n        (\"G5\",\"crypto_box/, crypto_kx/, crypto_scalarmult/, crypto_sign/, crypto_core/{ed25519,ristretto255}\"),\n        (\"G6\",\"randombytes/, crypto_kem/, crypto_ipcrypt/\")]\n\ndef rows(path):\n    out=[]\n    for ln in open(path):\n        ln=ln.rstrip(\"\\n\")\n        if ln.strip().startswith(\"|\") and ln.count(\"|\")>=4:\n            out.append(ln.strip())\n    return out\n\n# ---------------- ERRORS.md ----------------\nhdr = \"\"\"# ERRORS.md — error-surface table (Phase A / gate for Phase C)\n\nDerived mechanically from the C sources in `c_src/libsodium` by grepping every\n`return -1`, `return NULL`, failure-`return 0`, `ARGON2_*` error enum,\n`sodium_misuse()`, `abort()`, `assert(`, explicit range/size/overflow check,\nnull check and `errno =` site, then reading the surrounding code to state the\nexact triggering condition.\n\n**Response classes.** libsodium rejects input in three observably different\nways, and a differential test must distinguish them:\n\n1. **return value** — `-1`, `NULL`, `0`-as-failure. Compared directly.\n2. **`errno` side effect** — `ERANGE`, `EINVAL`, `ENOMEM`, `ENOSYS`, `EPERM`.\n   Both libraries share the calling thread's `errno`, so the harness zeroes it,\n   calls, and compares (`tests/common/mod.rs::errno`).\n3. **process death** — `sodium_misuse()` (which always ends in `abort()`),\n   `assert()`, `_out_of_bounds()` (`raise(SIGSEGV)`). Compared by re-executing\n   the test binary in a child process against one library at a time and\n   comparing the child's exit code / terminating signal\n   (`tests/common/mod.rs::diff_abort_case`).\n\n**Build configuration.** The reference C build defines no `HAVE_*` macros, so\n`HAVE_MLOCK`, `HAVE_MPROTECT`/`HAVE_PAGE_PROTECTION`, `HAVE_ALIGNED_MALLOC`,\n`HAVE_AMD64_ASM`, `HAVE_TMMINTRIN_H`/`HAVE_WMMINTRIN_H` and `HAVE_ARMCRYPTO`\nare all **off**. Rows guarded by those macros are marked as configuration\ndependent; the tests assert C/Rust *agreement* rather than a hard-coded value,\nso they stay correct either way.\n\n| # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result |\n|---|----------|----------------------------------------------|-------------------|\n\"\"\"\nn=0\nbody=[]\ncounts={}\nfor g,desc in groups:\n    rs=rows(f\"{L}/frag/{g}_errors.md\")\n    counts[g]=len(rs)\n    for r in rs:\n        parts=[p.strip() for p in r.strip(\"|\").split(\"|\")]\n        # parts[0] is the group tag\n        while len(parts)<4: parts.append(\"\")\n        n+=1\n        body.append(f\"| {n} | `{parts[1]}` | {parts[2]} | {parts[3]} |\")\nopen(f\"{T}/ERRORS.md\",\"w\").write(hdr+\"\\n\".join(body)+\"\\n\\n## Rows per module group\\n\\n| group | modules | rows |\\n|---|---|---|\\n\"+\n    \"\\n\".join(f\"| {g} | {d} | {counts[g]} |\" for g,d in groups)+f\"\\n| **total** | | **{n}** |\\n\")\nprint(\"ERRORS.md rows:\",n)\n\n# ---------------- CONFIGS.md ----------------\nhdr2 = \"\"\"# CONFIGS.md — configuration-surface table (Phase A / gate for Phase B)\n\nThe mirror of `ERRORS.md` for VALID input. Derived mechanically from the C\nsources and the public headers in `c_src/libsodium/include/sodium/`: every\nruntime option / mode / flag the public API can set, every distinct input\nSHAPE the code special-cases (sizes, block/rate boundaries, empty / one / many,\nchunk splits, counter values, primitive selection), and the FULL set of public\nentry points — including the lowest-level ones (`*_afternm`, `*_beforenm`,\n`*_detached`, `*_xor_ic`, the NaCl zero-padded forms, `init`/`update`/`final`\nstreaming APIs, `*_ll`), not just the one-shot convenience wrappers.\n\nEach row is one combination the C code treats differently. Rows are exercised\nwith MANY randomized inputs from a fixed seed (`tests/common/mod.rs::Rng`), not\na single hand-picked value.\n\nNon-deterministic entry points (`*_keygen`, `*_keypair`, `*_random`,\n`randombytes_buf`, `crypto_box_seal`, `crypto_secretstream_*_init_push`, ...)\nare made comparable by installing one deterministic `randombytes_implementation`\ninto BOTH libraries via `randombytes_set_implementation`\n(`tests/common/mod.rs::install_det_random`), so both observe the identical\nrandom stream.\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n\"\"\"\nn2=0\nbody2=[]\ncounts2={}\nfor g,desc in groups:\n    rs=rows(f\"{L}/frag/{g}_configs.md\")\n    counts2[g]=len(rs)\n    for r in rs:\n        parts=[p.strip() for p in r.strip(\"|\").split(\"|\")]\n        while len(parts)<4: parts.append(\"[ ]\")\n        n2+=1\n        body2.append(f\"| {n2} | {parts[1]} | {parts[2]} | [ ] |\")\nopen(f\"{T}/CONFIGS.md\",\"w\").write(hdr2+\"\\n\".join(body2)+\"\\n\\n## Rows per module group\\n\\n| group | modules | rows |\\n|---|---|---|\\n\"+\n    \"\\n\".join(f\"| {g} | {d} | {counts2[g]} |\" for g,d in groups)+f\"\\n| **total** | | **{n2}** |\\n\")\nprint(\"CONFIGS.md rows:\",n2)\nPY\nwc -l $W/translation/ERRORS.md $W/translation/CONFIGS.md; head -3 $W/translation/CONFIGS.md; grep -c \"^| [0-9]\" $W/translation/ERRORS.md $W/translation/CONFIGS.md","description":"Assemble ERRORS.md and CONFIGS.md artifacts"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":774,"cache_read_input_tokens":145614,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":774,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37babf23-64fa-4bd5-8c90-ef1a4034e89f","uuid":"26d11189-951e-4365-a8a2-7f6f96e9cd68","timestamp":"2026-09-08T15:21:22.029Z"}
