n  #[test]\n  fn zz_abort_child() {\n      let Some((case, is_c)) = child_case() else { return };\n      let l = libs(); let h = if is_c { l.c } else { l.rs };\n      // dlsym from `h`, perform the dangerous call for `case`\n      std::process::exit(0); // reached only if it did NOT abort\n  }\n  ```\n  `$ROOT/translation/tests/t02_g1_errors.rs` is a complete working example — COPY ITS STRUCTURE.\n\nStudy `$ROOT/translation/tests/t01_g1_utils.rs` (valid-path style) and `t02_g1_errors.rs` (error-path style) as templates.\n\n## YOUR SCOPE — module group G4\nC modules: `crypto_aead/` (aegis128l, aegis256, aes256gcm, chacha20poly1305 original+ietf, xchacha20poly1305), `crypto_secretbox/` (xsalsa20poly1305, xchacha20poly1305), `crypto_secretstream/`, `crypto_stream/` (chacha20 ref + ietf, salsa20, salsa2012, salsa208, xsalsa20, xchacha20), `crypto_core/` salsa20/salsa2012/salsa208/hsalsa20/hchacha20.\n\nYour Phase A tables (already produced, DO NOT EDIT THEM):\n- `$ROOT/translation/CONFIGS.md` rows **510-716** are yours.\n- `$ROOT/translation/ERRORS.md` rows **405-508** are yours.\nRead those row ranges. Each row must end up covered by a test.\n\nFacts already established about THIS build (no `HAVE_*` macros are defined):\n- `crypto_aead_aes256gcm_is_available()` returns 0, and ALL 9 aes256gcm entry points (encrypt/decrypt, both detached, `beforenm`, all four `_afternm`) unconditionally set `errno = ENOSYS` and return `-1`. They do NOT abort. The constant getters and `crypto_aead_aes256gcm_keygen` still work; `statebytes()` = 512. Test that this exact behaviour matches.\n- `*_encrypt_detached` in aegis aborts on oversized mlen/adlen while `*_decrypt_detached` returns `-1` for the same overflow — an asymmetry that must be reproduced.\n- The only `ic` guard is `crypto_stream_chacha20_ietf_xor_ic` (`ic > 2^32 - ceil(mlen/64)` → abort). `crypto_salsa20*` has no length checks at all.\n- `crypto_secretstream_..._push` performs NO tag validation: any byte 0x00-0xFF is accepted; only bit `0x02` (REKEY) is interpreted.\n- There are no runtime NULL checks anywhere in G4 (`__attribute__((nonnull))` is compile-time only), so do NOT pass NULL where the C dereferences.\n\n## YOUR DELIVERABLES\nCreate exactly two files:\n1. `$ROOT/translation/tests/t05_g4_aead.rs` — Phase B valid-path tests for CONFIGS.md rows 510-716.\n2. `$ROOT/translation/tests/t06_g4_aead_errors.rs` — Phase C error-path tests for ERRORS.md rows 405-508, plus generic boundaries (zero and oversized lengths, one step past every documented range, out-of-range tag/flag ints across FFI).\n\nRequirements:\n- EVERY test calls BOTH libraries via `pair::<F>(...)` and compares outputs byte-for-byte and return values. NEVER call Rust code directly.\n- Exercise the LOW-LEVEL entry points directly, not only wrappers: `*_encrypt_detached`/`*_decrypt_detached`; the aes256gcm precomputed-state API (`beforenm`, `encrypt_afternm`, `decrypt_afternm`, `encrypt_detached_afternm`, `decrypt_detached_afternm`); the NaCl zero-padded `crypto_secretbox()` / `crypto_secretbox_open()` (ZEROBYTES/BOXZEROBYTES form) and `crypto_secretbox_detached`/`_open_detached`; `crypto_secretstream_xchacha20poly1305_init_push/push/init_pull/pull/rekey`; every `crypto_stream_*` in all three forms (`_xor`, `_xor_ic`, plain keystream `crypto_stream_x(c,clen,n,k)`); `crypto_core_salsa20/salsa2012/salsa208` and `crypto_core_hsalsa20/hchacha20` with NULL and non-NULL constant `c`.\n- MANY randomized inputs per configuration, FIXED seed. Message lengths must include 0,1,15,16,17,31,32,33,63,64,65,127,128,129,1000; ad lengths 0,1,15,16,17,large; `ic` values 0,1,2,0xffff,0xffffffff-1,0xffffffff (and 64-bit ic for non-ietf variants).\n- For decryption, test BOTH the valid case and the tampered case (flip one bit in ct, in the mac, in the nonce, in the ad) — the -1 must match. Also test `m == NULL` verify-only mode where the C accepts it (every AEAD `*_decrypt_detached` and secretbox `*_open_detached`), but NOT for `crypto_secretstream_*_pull`, which unconditionally writes `m`.\n- Secretstream: multi-message sequences, tags MESSAGE(0)/PUSH(1)/REKEY(2)/FINAL(3) and out-of-range tag bytes, explicit `rekey()`, with and without ad, and pull returning the tag byte.\n- Add a comment on each test naming the CONFIGS.md / ERRORS.md row numbers it covers.\n\n## WHEN A TEST FAILS\nThe C is ALWAYS right. Fix the Rust in `$ROOT/translation/src/`. Relevant Rust files: `aead_aegis128l.rs`, `aead_aegis256.rs`, `aead_aes256gcm.rs`, `aead_chacha20poly1305.rs`, `aead_xchacha20poly1305.rs`, `secretbox.rs`, `secretstream.rs`, `crypto_stream.rs`, `stream_chacha20.rs`, `stream_salsa20.rs`, `core_salsa.rs`, `core_hsalsa20.rs`, `core_hchacha20.rs`, `poly1305.rs`, `softaes.rs`. Read the corresponding C file, find the exact discrepancy, fix the Rust, rerun. Never weaken a test to make it pass; never \"fix\" the C.\nIf a test of yours encodes a WRONG expectation (you assumed a check exists that the C does not perform), change the TEST to assert C/Rust agreement instead of your assumption, and note it in a comment.\n\n## FINISH CRITERIA\n`./dt.sh --test t05_g4_aead -- --test-threads=1` and `./dt.sh --test t06_g4_aead_errors -- --test-threads=1` both report `test result: ok` with 0 failures, covering CONFIGS.md 510-716 and ERRORS.md 405-508.\n\nReport back: the two file paths, the number of `#[test]` functions in each, the final `test result:` lines, any rows you could NOT cover (with reasons), and every change you made under translation/src/ (file + what was wrong + the fix).","outputFile":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-CIX3GT/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-li83Jg/37babf23-64fa-4bd5-8c90-ef1a4034e89f/tasks/aa5d8d2b1c1c98f61.output","canReadOutputFile":true}}
