{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Ux2DNsHSNDcxEenpqFCHQg","type":"tool_result","content":"# CONFIGS.md — configuration-surface table (Phase A / gate for Phase B)\n\nThe mirror of `ERRORS.md` for VALID input. Derived mechanically from the C\nsources and the public headers in `c_src/libsodium/include/sodium/`: every\nruntime option / mode / flag the public API can set, every distinct input\nSHAPE the code special-cases (sizes, block/rate boundaries, empty / one / many,\nchunk splits, counter values, primitive selection), and the FULL set of public\nentry points — including the lowest-level ones (`*_afternm`, `*_beforenm`,\n`*_detached`, `*_xor_ic`, the NaCl zero-padded forms, `init`/`update`/`final`\nstreaming APIs, `*_ll`), not just the one-shot convenience wrappers.\n\nEach row is one combination the C code treats differently. Rows are exercised\nwith MANY randomized inputs from a fixed seed (`tests/common/mod.rs::Rng`), not\na single hand-picked value.\n\nNon-deterministic entry points (`*_keygen`, `*_keypair`, `*_random`,\n`randombytes_buf`, `crypto_box_seal`, `crypto_secretstream_*_init_push`, ...)\nare made comparable by installing one deterministic `randombytes_implementation`\ninto BOTH libraries via `randombytes_set_implementation`\n(`tests/common/mod.rs::install_det_random`), so both observe the identical\nrandom stream.\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 1 | sodium_init | first call in the process (initialized == 0): full CPU-feature probe + randombytes_stir + alloc init + impl picking | [ ] |\n| 2 | sodium_init | second and subsequent calls (initialized != 0): idempotency path returning 1 | [ ] |\n| 3 | sodium_init, sodium_set_misuse_handler | sodium_set_misuse_handler(NULL) then sodium_init(), handler stays NULL | [ ] |\n| 4 | sodium_set_misuse_handler | set a non-NULL handler, then replace it with a second non-NULL handler, then reset to NULL | [ ] |\n| 5 | sodium_crit_enter, sodium_crit_leave | balanced enter/leave pair (locked 0 -> 1 -> 0) | [ ] |\n| 6 | sodium_version_string | no arguments; must equal \"1.0.23\" | [ ] |\n| 7 | sodium_library_version_major | no arguments; must equal 30 | [ ] |\n| 8 | sodium_library_version_minor | no arguments; must equal 0 | [ ] |\n| 9 | sodium_library_minimal | non-minimal build (SODIUM_LIBRARY_MINIMAL undefined) -> 0 | [ ] |\n| 10 | sodium_library_minimal | minimal build (SODIUM_LIBRARY_MINIMAL defined) -> 1 | [ ] |\n| 11 | sodium_runtime_has_neon | after sodium_init() on x86-64 (expect 0); getter is a pure struct read, must be stable across repeated calls | [ ] |\n| 12 | sodium_runtime_has_armcrypto | after sodium_init(); 0 unless has_neon and ARM crypto extensions detected | [ ] |\n| 13 | sodium_runtime_has_sse2 | after sodium_init(); HAVE_EMMINTRIN_H build vs not (compile-time forced 0) | [ ] |\n| 14 | sodium_runtime_has_sse3 | after sodium_init(); HAVE_PMMINTRIN_H build vs not | [ ] |\n| 15 | sodium_runtime_has_ssse3 | after sodium_init(); HAVE_TMMINTRIN_H build vs not | [ ] |\n| 16 | sodium_runtime_has_sse41 | after sodium_init(); HAVE_SMMINTRIN_H build vs not | [ ] |\n(eval):1: ================= not found","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01U8VethqMiRTDcWo7B6zhob","session_id":"37babf23-64fa-4bd5-8c90-ef1a4034e89f","uuid":"ee42aae3-8f09-483f-bd41-bf512f4ff217","timestamp":"2026-09-08T15:24:34.169Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write G4 AEAD/stream differential tests"}
