{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_jkhhotyfrwtkwuz7ngmebl4sqqoedpljy6azj3ucpkdxugpreg5a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both suites are green. Final verification complete.\n\n## Deliverables\n\n**Files created** (nothing else was added or modified):\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-li83Jg/translation/tests/t05_g4_aead.rs` — **65** `#[test]` functions (Phase B, CONFIGS.md rows 510‑716)\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-li83Jg/translation/tests/t06_g4_aead_errors.rs` — **32** `#[test]` functions incl. `zz_abort_child` (Phase C, ERRORS.md rows 405‑508)\n\n**Final results**\n```\n./dt.sh --test t05_g4_aead -- --test-threads=1\ntest result: ok. 65 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 1.42s\n\n./dt.sh --test t06_g4_aead_errors -- --test-threads=1\ntest result: ok. 32 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 49.10s\n```\nPre-existing suites still pass (t00: 4, t01: 18, t02: 18, all ok).\n\n## Changes under translation/src/\n**None.** The Rust translation of every G4 module matched the C byte-for-byte on the first run — encrypt/decrypt (combined + detached), the aes256gcm ENOSYS stubs and precomputed-state API, the NaCl zero-padded secretbox, secretstream push/pull/rekey (including raw 52-byte state comparison), all `crypto_stream_*` forms, and all five `crypto_core_*` primitives.\n\nBecause \"everything passed\" is a suspicious result, I mutation-tested the pipeline: changing `while i < 10` → `< 9` in `src/core_hchacha20.rs` made `c714_716_core_hchacha20` fail with a hex diff at byte 0, proving `dt.sh` rebuilds the cdylib and the harness really loads two distinct libraries. The mutation was reverted (`while i < 10` restored, test green again).\n\n## Coverage notes\n- Every CONFIGS row 510‑716 and ERRORS row 405‑508 is named in a test comment (row 525/526/528/532/533 are named in the `c521_524_525_526_528_532_533_aegis128l_pointer_modes` function name/comment).\n- Abort rows are compared via `diff_abort_case` with `messagebytes_max() + 1` computed inside the child, i.e. exactly one step past each documented range: rows 405‑407, 415‑417, 442, 448, 454, 460, 466, 476, 480, 487, 488, 489.\n- Row 489 (the module's only `ic` guard) is tested on **both** sides of the boundary: `(ic, mlen)` = (2³²−1, 65/128/129), (2³²−2, 129/1000), (2³²−3, 193) abort identically; (2³²−1, 0/1/63/64), (2³²−2, 65/128) exit 0 identically.\n- The `*_encrypt_detached` aborts vs `*_decrypt_detached` returns `-1` asymmetry for the same overflow is reproduced explicitly (`e410_411`, `e420_421`).\n\n**Rows that cannot be exhaustively triggered** (each documented in a test comment, with the strongest available agreement assertion substituted):\n- **414, 424** — `aegis*_mac` with `maclen ∉ {16,32}`: unreachable, `maclen` is hard-wired to `ABYTES`; test asserts `abytes() == 32` in both libs.\n- **425(partly), 435‑441** — the aesni/armcrypto AES‑GCM implementation is compiled out; asserted via `is_available() == 0` plus `-1`/`ENOSYS` for exactly the inputs those rows describe (oversized `ad_len`/`m_len`, forged mac, `clen < ABYTES`).\n- **478** — the 32-bit secretstream counter wrap needs ~2³² pushes. Instead the *mechanism* is verified: 4-byte little-endian counter, +1 per push, reset to 1 on rekey, identical in both libs (plus a 400-message run in t05 row 655).\n- **482** — `pull` with `m == NULL` is UB (no verify-only mode); deliberately not exercised per instructions; the test asserts the contrast (AEAD/secretbox accept `m == NULL`, secretstream has no such mode).\n- **484‑486, 490‑492, 500, 501** — these compare an `unsigned long long` against `SODIUM_SIZE_MAX = min(UINT64_MAX, SIZE_MAX) = UINT64_MAX`, so no argument value can trigger the misuse. `e484_492_500_501_...` instead differentially compares the caps themselves (all must be `usize::MAX`), which is what makes the path unreachable.\n- **507** — no runtime NULL checks exist; only the intentionally-nullable pointers are exercised (`nsec` NULL and non-NULL must give identical output, all `*_p` out-params NULL, `ad == NULL` with `adlen == 0`, core `c == NULL`, `m == NULL` verify-only).\n- **508** — n/a (no weak-key rejection in G4); asserted positively: all-zero and all-0xff keys/nonces are accepted identically."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2121,"cache_read_input_tokens":260861,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2121,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01U8VethqMiRTDcWo7B6zhob","session_id":"37babf23-64fa-4bd5-8c90-ef1a4034e89f","uuid":"51233351-b605-424d-93f0-da214723642b","timestamp":"2026-09-08T15:52:46.951Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write G4 AEAD/stream differential tests"}
