{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ftjcxvlonm6d2ku2bgwbzec6xnauem55uhjafelcpdkugmalyplq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both suites pass. Final report:\n\n## Files delivered\n\n**`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-li83Jg/translation/tests/t07_g5_asym.rs`** — Phase B, valid paths, **23 `#[test]` functions**\n```\ntest result: ok. 23 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 3.30s\n```\n\n**`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-li83Jg/translation/tests/t08_g5_asym_errors.rs`** — Phase C, error paths + generic boundaries, **20 `#[test]` functions** (incl. `zz_abort_child`)\n```\ntest result: ok. 20 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 22.77s\n```\n\n## Changes under `translation/src/`\n**None.** The Rust translation matched the C bit-for-bit on every one of the ~200k differential calls across all of G5 — `crypto_box` (all three primitive families incl. NaCl zero-padded, easy/detached, afternm, seal), `crypto_kx`, `crypto_scalarmult` (curve25519/ed25519/ristretto255, clamped and noclamp), `crypto_sign` (detached, combined, ed25519ph streaming, key conversions), and the whole `crypto_core_ed25519_*` / `crypto_core_ristretto255_*` surface (points, scalar arithmetic, `from_string`/`from_hash`), including all abort paths.\n\n**Harness bite verified:** I temporarily inserted `t_[0] ^= 1` into `crypto_core_ed25519_scalar_negate` in `src/core_ed25519.rs`, confirmed `g5_core_ed25519_scalars` failed with a C/Rust hex diff, then reverted (byte-identical restore confirmed, no `TEMPORARY MUTATION` markers remain). So the zero-divergence result is real, not a vacuous pass.\n\n## Coverage\nAll CONFIGS rows 717-888 and all ERRORS rows 509-638 are referenced by comment and exercised.\n\n## Rows where the Phase-A table's stated expectation was WRONG (test changed to assert C/Rust agreement, noted in a comment)\n- **CONFIGS 766** — pairs the RFC 7748 §5.2 *input scalar* `a546e36b…` with the §6.1 *Alice public key* `8520f009…`; they don't belong together. Replaced with the real §6.1 Alice **and** Bob vectors (both verified against C); `a546e36b…` is still exercised.\n- **CONFIGS 778** — claims `base_noclamp(8) == base(1)`. False: `_crypto_scalarmult_ed25519_clamp` does `k[0] &= 248; k[31] |= 64`, so `base(1)` multiplies by 2^254. Replaced with the real invariant `base(n) == base_noclamp(clamp(n))`, asserted for `n = 1` and 250 random `n`.\n- **CONFIGS 870** — the literal `3066f82a…` is not what 1.0.23 produces for `from_hash(SHA512(\"Ristretto is traditionally a small shot of espresso coffee\"))` (the draft tabulates the 64-byte map input, not a pre-image). Reduced to C/Rust agreement + `is_valid_point == 1`.\n- **CONFIGS 838/839/875/876** — `scalar_add(s, negate(s)) == 0` / `+ complement(s) == 1` hold only for **canonical** inputs: `crypto_core_ed25519_scalar_add` calls `sodium_add(x_, y_, 32)`, discarding the carry out of bit 255. The identities are now asserted for canonical inputs; non-canonical inputs (e.g. all-`0xff`) still flow through every entry point with C/Rust agreement asserted.\n- **ERRORS 586** — my first draft asserted `sig[63] & 240 == 0` for a `sig[63] & 224` probe; impossible since `0xe0 ⊂ 0xf0`. Rewritten with the correct reasoning (any `S` with a bit of `0xe0` set is ≥ 2^253 > L, so never canonical ⇒ the `ED25519_COMPAT` branch is behaviourally indistinguishable from the live check) and all four high bit patterns probed.\n\n## Rows not separately reachable (documented in-test, not skipped silently)\n- **ERRORS 517/518** — `d |= q[i]` all-zero ladder output and `implementation->mult() != 0`; both `LCOV_EXCL` and unreachable from the public API (every small-order `p` is caught by `has_small_order` first; ref10 `mult` always returns 0). A 600-case random sweep asserts return-value agreement regardless of which branch fires.\n- **ERRORS 589** — `smlen - 64 > SODIUM_SIZE_MAX - 64` requires `smlen > SIZE_MAX`, unrepresentable in `unsigned long long` on this target.\n- **ERRORS 591** — `crypto_sign_ed25519_detached` has no failure path, so the combined-sign error branch is unreachable; asserted 0 for 63 arbitrary `sk` values incl. all-zero and all-`0xff`.\n- **ERRORS 616/617/618** — `_string_to_points(n > 2)`, `assert(h_len <= 0xff)`, `ge25519_xmont_to_ymont` failure: all `LCOV_EXCL` `abort()`/`assert()` sites with no public entry point. The three sizes that feed row 617 are pinned instead.\n- **ERRORS 638** — confirmed by `has_sym` that `crypto_core_ed25519_from_uniform`/`_from_hash` are absent and that `_from_string{,_nu}` / `crypto_core_ristretto255_from_hash` are present.\n\n## Confirmed-as-designed C quirks reproduced (not \"fixed\")\n`crypto_core_ed25519_add/sub` accept non-canonical, identity and small-order encodings (609); `scalar_invert` returns 0 for `s = L`/`2L` (613/635); `crypto_scalarmult_ed25519{,_base}(n=0)` clobbers `q` before returning −1 (524/527); `crypto_box_seal` writes `c[0..32]` even on −1 and leaves `c[32..]` untouched (566); `pk_to_curve25519` omits the `ge25519_is_canonical` check that `verify_detached` performs (595); a single NULL `rx`/`tx` in `crypto_kx_*_session_keys` is valid, only both-NULL aborts (574/575); `crypto_box` accepts a non-zero-padded message (563)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":272,"cache_read_input_tokens":271893,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":272,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01QiaBM6Z2JFrEYVe6tn7un9","session_id":"37babf23-64fa-4bd5-8c90-ef1a4034e89f","uuid":"f510c647-cbd6-42dd-8d53-0de70eb8161b","timestamp":"2026-09-08T15:55:45.828Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write G5 asymmetric differential tests"}
