{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a5e2e2ba5235e0096","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01YFsDeJBuv2gUaUX1ftWW4d","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-CIX3GT/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-li83Jg/37babf23-64fa-4bd5-8c90-ef1a4034e89f/tasks/a5e2e2ba5235e0096.output","summary":"Both files are green.\n\n## Deliverables\n\n**`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-li83Jg/translation/tests/t03_g3_hash.rs`** — 23 `#[test]` functions (Phase B, CONFIGS.md 281-509)\n```\ntest result: ok. 23 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.66s\n```\n\n**`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-li83Jg/translation/tests/t04_g3_hash_errors.rs`** — 13 `#[test]` functions (Phase C, ERRORS.md 282-404; one of them is the `zz_abort_child` re-exec driver)\n```\ntest result: ok. 13 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 152.93s\n```\n\nEvery call goes through `pair::<F>()`/dlsym into both `.so`s; low-level entry points are exercised directly (`crypto_generichash_blake2b_init_salt_personal/_update/_final`, `crypto_hash_sha3*_init/update/final`, `crypto_xof_*_init_with_domain/_update/_squeeze`, `crypto_kdf_hkdf_*_extract_init/_extract_update/_extract_final/_expand`, `crypto_auth_hmacsha*_init/_update/_final`, `crypto_onetimeauth_poly1305_init/_update/_final`, `crypto_core_keccak1600_*`, the exported `_sodium_blake2b*` internals, the `crypto_onetimeauth_poly1305_donna_implementation` vtable, and both `*_pick_best_implementation` hooks). State buffers are sized from `*_statebytes()` and 64-byte aligned; only outputs/return values are compared for the opaque `*_state` types (noted in the file header), except keccak1600 where the C treats the state as a plain LE byte array so raw state bytes are compared too.\n\n## Change made under translation/src/\n\n`src/blake2b.rs`, `crypto_generichash_blake2b_final` — **was wrong**: it did `outlen as u8`, silently truncating, so `crypto_generichash_blake2b_final(state, out, 288)` returned 0 and wrote 32 bytes while the C (built with an empty `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE`, i.e. no `-DNDEBUG`, so `assert()` is live) hit `assert(outlen <= UINT8_MAX)` and died with SIGABRT. **Fix**: added the guard before the truncation, using the crate's existing convention for C `assert`/`abort`:\n```rust\n/* assert(outlen <= UINT8_MAX); */\nif outlen > u8::MAX as usize {\n    crate::csys::abort();\n}\n```\nThat was the only divergence found; no other `src/` file was touched.\n\n## Rows not covered by an executed call (and why)\n\nCONFIGS.md — all of 281-509 covered. Caveat on **393**: `keccak1600_armsha3_*` is `#ifdef __ARM_FEATURE_SHA3`-only and is not compiled into this x86 build, so the test asserts that the `_sodium_keccak1600_ref_*` backend is byte-identical to the `crypto_core_keccak1600_*` dispatch in both libraries instead.\n\nERRORS.md — the following are not executable by construction; each is documented in a doc-comment on the covering test:\n- **285** dead branch (`inlen > UINT64_MAX` with `inlen` already `unsigned long long`).\n- **286, 298, 316, 322, 329, 336** `LCOV_EXCL`/unreachable inner-failure returns (`blake2b_init*` only ever returns 0 or aborts) and asserts guarded by the preceding `> 64` checks.\n- **306** internal invariant `assert(S->buflen <= BLAKE2B_BLOCKBYTES)` — not violable from outside.\n- **337, 338, 371, 379, 398** `COMPILER_ASSERT` / compile-time only.\n- **339, 345, 351, 364, 370, 380, 402** genuine NULL dereferences of `nonnull` parameters (`state`/`out`/`in`/`ctx`) — real UB with no observable rejection, so deliberately not executed. (Rows 355/356/383/385, which are also NULL derefs, *are* executed via `diff_abort_case` because the C reliably faults there and the differential comparison is meaningful; both libraries die identically.)\n- **394** the `(-(h == correct))` hardening term requires the caller's `h` to alias the library's internal stack buffer — unreachable through the public API.\n- **303** is asserted as C/Rust *agreement* rather than the table's \"silent truncation\": that behaviour is NDEBUG-only, and this C build has assertions enabled, so `outlen >= 256` aborts. Noted in a comment.\n\nOne operational note: `src/randombytes.rs` / `src/randombytes_internal.rs` were being edited concurrently by another agent during my runs, which trips the harness's `STALE Rust cdylib` mtime guard mid-run. Both final runs above are clean re-runs with no staleness panic.","usage":{"total_tokens":258289,"tool_uses":72,"duration_ms":2124713},"uuid":"fba3f6dc-3e80-41dc-b35f-5db98e6ed2c7","session_id":"37babf23-64fa-4bd5-8c90-ef1a4034e89f"}
