{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_fxfa6h54qotxmbxlagoi3crobpuojamug4ypeagm4rlvyyd3l2xa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**ALL CHECKS PASSED.** 349/349 differential tests green, 0 missing symbols, `c_src/` untouched (all sources still at their original 15:02–15:03 timestamps).\n\n## Completion gate\n\n| gate | result |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md`: `nm -D` diff | **890 = 890**, 0 missing, 0 extra, 0 undefined non-libc symbols |\n| Phase B: every `CONFIGS.md` row | **995/995** rows checked off, all passing across randomized inputs |\n| Phase C: every `ERRORS.md` row | **739/739** rows have a passing error-path differential test |\n| Binary stdout comparison | N/A — no `add_executable` in CMake, no `[[bin]]` in Cargo.toml |\n| Every feature combination | `Cargo.toml` declares no `[features]` → one configuration; `verify.sh` enumerates them mechanically so new ones are covered automatically |\n\n## 4 real bugs found and fixed in `translation/src`\n\n1. **`blake2b.rs`** — `crypto_generichash_blake2b_final` did `outlen as u8`, so `outlen=288` returned 0 and wrote 32 bytes; C hits `assert(outlen <= UINT8_MAX)` and SIGABRTs.\n2. **`randombytes_sysrandom.rs`** — missing `assert(chunk_size > 0)`; the public `.buf(ptr, 0)` vtable entry returned quietly in Rust, aborted in C.\n3. **`randombytes_internal.rs`** — same missing assert.\n4. **`argon2.rs` / `argon2_encoding.rs` / `pwhash_argon2.rs`** — `argon2_type` was a 2-variant `#[repr(C)] enum`, dropping C's reachable `default:` arms; an out-of-range `alg` (legal across FFI) returned `0` instead of `ARGON2_INCORRECT_TYPE`.\n\nBugs 1–3 were only visible because the reference C build has an empty `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE` — no `-DNDEBUG`, so C `assert()`s are live.\n\n## Why \"everything else matched\" is trustworthy, not vacuous\n\nI mutation-tested independently: 12 deliberate one-line breaks (AES round function, ed25519 sign bit, scrypt/blake2b/siphash rotations, HMAC ipad, ML-KEM Montgomery constant, ipcrypt degenerate-key branch, hex digit table…) were all caught, then reverted byte-identically. One mutant was *not* caught — `CRYPTO_STREAM_CHUNK 131072 → 65536` — which I analysed rather than papered over: it's an equivalent mutant (internal loop granularity, any multiple of 64 gives identical output). It did expose a real gap: no suite fed a message past that boundary, so I added `t14_large_inputs.rs` (131072±1/63/64/65, 2×131072, 400 000 bytes across every bulk entry point).\n\nI also found and narrowed two genuinely flaky assertions in the entropy suites (a single random byte is `0x00` one time in 256) — both now only applied at sizes where a false positive is 2⁻¹²⁸, re-run 5–6× clean.\n\n## Artifacts in `translation/`\n\n`SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md` (739 rows, each with the covering test), `CONFIGS.md` (995 rows), `VERIFICATION.md`, `dt.sh` (single suite; always rebuilds the cdylib), `verify.sh` (full gate), `tests/` (15 files, 349 tests) — plus `_logs/gen_tables.py` to regenerate the tables and the row→test mapping.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: `cargo test` alone does **not** rebuild a `cdylib`-only lib target, so a bare run silently tests a stale `.so`. The harness now panics with `STALE Rust cdylib` in that case, and `dt.sh`/`verify.sh` always build first."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":635,"cache_read_input_tokens":324060,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":635,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37babf23-64fa-4bd5-8c90-ef1a4034e89f","uuid":"18e4da4d-d3b4-4071-a12f-e1bc11bb2978","timestamp":"2026-09-08T17:19:42.311Z"}
